<title>USA: UAL's United to add new flights.</title>
<headline>UAL's United to add new flights.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Airlines, a unit of UAL Corp, said Monday it would strengthen service at Newark International Airport by adding new nonstop flights to both Boston and San Diego, Calif., effective January 7.</p>
<p>The carrier said it will operate four daily round-trip flights between Newark and Boston and a single daily round-trip flight between Newark and San Diego.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
